# try-no.psv -- programs whose card gets NO "Try it" button.  name | why
#
# Try It appears only on cards that can actually be run.
# Every card here WAS captured running, under the same emulator the browser
# page runs -- so this list is not about what fails.  It is the programs
# whose job needs something no browser tab has: a serial line, a modem, a
# printer, a network peer, an X server, a real disk drive, the system clock,
# or system state.  Trying one would show only its refusal, which the card
# already shows.  tools/tryable.py reads this; check_disk fails on a name
# that is not a card.
qp|hands its command to a shell with options only the EFFO shell took; no shell here runs it
splman|the print spooler's manager: there is no printer
splprt|the print spooler's printer process: there is no printer
lprm|removes a print job: there is no printer
lpq|shows the print queue: there is no printer
lpshut|stops the print spooler: there is no printer
disktest|measures a real disk drive
trap|a trap handler, which only system state can install
puzzle|a G-Windows program
uucico|talks to a UUCP peer over a serial line
msntp|sets the clock from a network time server
ttcp|measures throughput between two networked machines
nslookup|looks names up on a network name server
nsquery|looks a host up on a network name server
blastem|XMODEM and YMODEM over a modem
disable|switches off a serial port's monitor
enable|switches on a serial port's monitor
setfont|loads a font into a terminal that takes downloadable fonts
sbreak|sends a break on a serial line
basicwin|an X11 program
xengine|an X11 program
transfer|reads a GDOS disk drive
mvolformat|formats floppy disks
dpark|parks a disk drive's heads
setime|sets the system clock, which a browser tab cannot move
xy|receives a file over a modem line
xyt|wants a modem port
tterm|wants a modem port
k|receives a file from a Kermit sender on the line
infoxpress|reaches its host over a serial line
inetdc|serves a network connection that inetd hands it
authwn|authenticates a web request that a server hands it
elvprsv|runs when elvis dies, to save its buffer
g|an Atari GRAPH program written to run in supervisor state; from a shell it aborts
sine|an Atari GRAPH program written to run in supervisor state; from a shell it aborts
striche|an Atari GRAPH program written to run in supervisor state; from a shell it aborts
graphdemo|an Atari GRAPH program written to run in supervisor state; from a shell it aborts
graphsave|an Atari GRAPH program written to run in supervisor state; from a shell it aborts
showpic|an Atari GRAPH program written to run in supervisor state; from a shell it aborts
